# {{ project.name }}

A [Laravel 13](https://laravel.com) web app with an [Inertia](https://inertiajs.com) frontend in {% if vue %}[Vue 3](https://vuejs.org){% else %}[React 19](https://react.dev){% endif %} and TypeScript, styled with {% if choices.css == "tailwind" %}[Tailwind CSS 4](https://tailwindcss.com){% elif choices.css == "bootstrap" %}[Bootstrap 5](https://getbootstrap.com){% else %}plain CSS{% endif %}, on {{ dbname }}.

## Requirements
{% if full %}
- Docker 24 or newer with Docker Compose. PHP, Composer, Node.js{% if choices.database != "sqlite" %} and {{ dbname }}{% endif %} run in containers; nothing else is needed on this machine.
{%- else %}
- PHP 8.4 or newer with the `pdo_{% if choices.database == "postgres" %}pgsql{% elif choices.database == "mysql" %}mysql{% else %}sqlite{% endif %}` extension, and [Composer](https://getcomposer.org) 2 (on macOS: `brew install php composer`, or [Laravel Herd](https://herd.laravel.com))
- Node.js 24 or newer
{%- if choices.docker == "run" %}
- Docker 24 or newer with Docker Compose ({% if choices.database != "sqlite" %}for the {{ dbname }} server and {% endif %}for running the production container)
{%- elif choices.database == "postgres" %}
- A PostgreSQL server (e.g. `brew install postgresql@18` or [Postgres.app](https://postgresapp.com)) with a database for this app
{%- elif choices.database == "mysql" %}
- A MySQL server (e.g. `brew install mysql`) with a database for this app
{%- endif %}
{%- endif %}

## Quick start

```sh
[ -f .env ] || cp .env.example .env   # first run after cloning
{%- if full %}
docker compose build dev
docker compose run --rm dev composer install
docker compose run --rm dev npm ci
docker compose run --rm dev php artisan key:generate
docker compose run --rm dev php artisan migrate
docker compose up dev
{%- else %}
composer install
npm ci
php artisan key:generate
{%- if choices.docker == "run" and choices.database != "sqlite" %}
docker compose up -d --wait db        # the {{ dbname }} server
{%- elif choices.database != "sqlite" %}
# create the database and set DB_* in .env first
{%- endif %}
php artisan migrate
composer dev
{%- endif %}
```

Open http://localhost:{{ ports.APP_PORT }}. The Vite dev server (port {{ ports.VITE_PORT }}) reloads pages, components and styles as you edit them. The **Notes** page is a small example feature that goes through every layer: route → controller → form request → service → model → migration, and an Inertia page with components.

## Commands
{% if full %}
Run them in the dev container: `docker compose run --rm dev <command>`.
{% endif %}
| Command | What it does |
| --- | --- |
| `{% if full %}docker compose up dev{% else %}composer dev{% endif %}` | PHP server and Vite with hot reload |
| `composer check` | Everything that must pass before a commit: Pint, Larastan, PHPUnit, ESLint, Prettier, TypeScript |
| `composer test` | PHPUnit tests |
| `composer format` | Fix formatting (Pint, ESLint, Prettier) |
| `npm run build` | Production build of the frontend into `public/build` |
| `php artisan migrate` | Apply database migrations |
| `php artisan db:seed` | Add sample notes |
{%- if choices.docker != "none" %}
| `docker compose up --build{% if full %} app{% endif %}` | Build and run the production container on http://localhost:{{ ports.APP_PORT }} |
{%- endif %}

## Configuration

All settings live in `.env` in the project root. It is git-ignored; `.env.example` documents every key and is committed.

| Key | Value | Description |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `APP_NAME` | `{{ env.APP_NAME }}` | App name in the header and page titles |
| `APP_URL` | `{{ env.APP_URL }}` | Public URL of the app |
| `APP_PORT` | `{{ ports.APP_PORT }}` | Port of the app{% if choices.docker != "none" %} (also the published container port){% endif %} |
| `VITE_PORT` | `{{ ports.VITE_PORT }}` | Port of the Vite dev server |
| `DB_CONNECTION` | `{{ env.DB_CONNECTION }}` | Database driver |
| `DB_DATABASE` | `{{ env.DB_DATABASE }}` | {% if choices.database == "sqlite" %}SQLite file, relative to the project root{% else %}Database name{% endif %} |
{%- if choices.database != "sqlite" %}
| `DB_HOST`, `DB_PORT` | `{{ env.DB_HOST }}`, `{{ env.DB_PORT }}` | {% if choices.docker == "none" %}Your database server{% elif full %}The `db` container (database tools on this machine: 127.0.0.1:`FORWARD_DB_PORT`){% else %}The `db` container as seen from this machine (the app container uses `db`){% endif %} |
| `DB_USERNAME`, `DB_PASSWORD` | `{{ env.DB_USERNAME }}`, … | Database credentials |
{%- endif %}
{%- if choices.docker != "none" %}
| `COMPOSE_PROJECT_NAME` | `{{ env.COMPOSE_PROJECT_NAME }}` | Prefix of the Docker containers, volumes and images |
| `DOCKER_DATA` | `{{ env.DOCKER_DATA }}` | Where containers keep the database: `data` (Docker volume) or `./data` (project folder) |
{%- endif %}

